{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>יוקח</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: ברזל מעפר יוקח, גם שבי גבור יוקח. Meaning: also the righteous captive will be taken from the mighty by merit of יוקח נא מעט מים. ברזל מעפר יוקח — meaning: iron, the sword of punishment, will be taken from Israel, who are likened to dust, by merit of Abraham who said ואנכי עפר ואפר, corresponding to יוקח נא מעט מים. By gematria: מכאן they merited the well." "<b> ורחצו רגליכם</b> Twice in the Masorah: here, and the other in this same pericope, by Lot. From here we learn that he was concerned about ע\"א (idolatry), for Lot preceded lodging to washing, and Abraham preceded washing to lodging — teaching that he was concerned lest they be Arabs and bring ע\"א into his house."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The gematria equation is stated elliptically: the phrase יוקח נא מעט מים equals מכאן זכו לבאר by gematria, but the numerical value is not written.", 1 "ע\"א read as עבודה זרה (idolatry); the Arabic reading of ערביים preserved as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:20.499550853Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}